PART 5: Hyperbolic geometry — formal group as polygon metric
======================================================================

n=4:
  regular polygon rapidity: atanh((n-2)/n) = 0.5*ln(3) = 0.5493
  this is the Riemannian distance from 0 to 0.5000 on the
  Poincaré line [-1,1] with metric ds = dx/(1-x^2)

  at t=1/4 (regular polygon):
    runner gaps: ['0.2500', '0.5000', '0.2500']...
    all gaps = 1/n = 0.2500: False
    rapidities: ['0.5493', '0.0000', '0.5493']...
    all rapidity = 0.5493: False

