The alignment defect is ALWAYS 4 for twin-Goldbach exceptions.
This means: the nearest miss is always exactly 4 away from a twin.
The "complement necklace" structure: the 11 K+K holes match
exactly the 11 exception triples (plus the initial pair {2,4}).
